<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Farabundo Martí National Liberation Front</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1980">1980</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as FMLN</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/farabundo-marti">Farabundo Martí</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-south-yemen">National Liberation Front</a> (FMLN) was formed in October 1980 as a coalition of five Salvadoran left-wing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> organisations and named after the communist leader Farabundo Martí. It fought the government in the civil war of 1980–1992, which ended with the Chapultepec Peace Accords. It then became a legal political party and held the presidency from 2009 to 2019.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/farabundo-marti-national-liberation-front.jpg" alt="Farabundo Martí National Liberation Front" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ivan Ch RU · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Logo_of_the_FMLN.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
